      "case": "G03-01",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "A and B were created through the UI in separate persistent browser profiles with the same password; public keys differ and both vaults store encrypted key material without password/nsec fields."
    },
    {
      "case": "G03-02",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "Persistent browser restart restored A only when requested; B required the correct password, rejected the wrong one without vault mutation, and manual lock cleared the session."
    },
    {
      "case": "G03-03",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "The UI exported an encrypted backup and a clean context imported the same public identity; it could reopen the contact using the other person’s public npub."
    },
    {
      "case": "G03-04",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "The public key shown in B profile opened A’s conversation; a valid nprofile preserved its local relay hint and did not connect automatically."
    },
    {
      "case": "G03-05",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "Empty, truncated, name-only, nsec and self contacts were rejected in Portuguese without closing the dialog, creating the wrong contact or changing identity."
    },
    {
      "case": "G03-06",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "Across creation, lock, backup, contact and recovery flows, the PWA completed no external HTTP request. Relay destinations were blocked by the local deny proxy; browser-background destinations were separately classified. Passwords/private keys were absent from Web Storage and no central login/recovery request was observed."
    },
    {
      "case": "G03-07",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "Profile sharing produced a Property link, NIP-19 profile and QR decoded independently; six active/locked-start intake cases prefilled the identity, stripped the contact fragment and created no conversation or message before confirmation."
    },
    {
      "case": "G03-08",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "The PWA required an encrypted backup acknowledgement, then replaced the active local key; it kept the previous Nostr identity and local history separate as the warning states."
    },
    {
      "case": "G03-09",
      "status": "PASS",
      "reason": "25 fixed browser journeys passed: 4 each for first use, returning sessions, manual lock/unlock, encrypted restore and corrupted vaults; 3 with zero relays and blocked sends; and 2 with IndexedDB denied. Identity/recovery labels matched in English and Portuguese and all setup, import and replacement controls were reached by keyboard."
    }
